.TH ANONYMOS-SYSCALLS 7 "2026-09-06" "EpinAnonymOS" "Overview"
.SH NAME
anonymos-syscalls \- the syscall surface of the EpinAnonymOS kernel
.SH DESCRIPTION
This kernel implements a SUBSET of the Linux x86-64 ABI so unmodified Linux binaries run,
plus a native object API on a syscall number outside the Linux range.
.PP
Counts below are generated from the kernel source, not maintained by hand, so they cannot
drift from what the kernel actually dispatches.
.SH DEVIATIONS THAT BITE
These differ from stock Linux and have each cost real debugging time:
.TP
AF_UNIX read
Returns EAGAIN on an empty socket instead of blocking.  A client that reads once and gives
up will lose the race; poll first.
.TP
open(2) on an absolute path
Resolved against the CALLING TASK's namespace.  A confined task sees ENOENT for an unbound
path and EACCES for an explicitly denied one.
.TP
connect(2) to an AF_UNIX socket
Refused with EACCES when it crosses identities without a broker rule.  Connections to a
system-trust peer (the compositor) are always allowed.
.TP
inotify
Watches only the writable runtime overlay.  A watch on an image file or a synthetic /proc
path succeeds and never fires.
